   --apply
 
+## Local Native hover commissioning (2026-11-04)
+
+The optional local profile uses the normal L2/L3/L4/L5 execution gates and the
+same six Native panels. From `TDOC_v20260911_2052`, after sourcing the environment
+and accepting an Offline handoff for the **current** source/configuration:
+
+```bash
+$PYTHON -m tddt_tdoc.cli --config configs/tdoc.yaml nav-online \
+  --reuse-existing-offline-knowledge --online-episodes 1 \
+  --online-max-cycles-per-episode 12 \
+  --online-local-hover-seconds 1 --online-local-hover-height-m 3
+```
+
+This selects `on_ground -> vertical_takeoff -> hover -> vertical_landing ->
+touchdown` around the surveyed origin. Normal route missions keep their eleven
+phases. Valid durations are 1..60 seconds and heights 1..10 metres. The duration
+counts measured, contiguous, executed control with accepted Layer7 feedback,
+within 5 metres horizontally and 1 metre vertically; ground time, missing
+feedback and gaps in execution coverage never count. Only increase the duration
+to 5/10/30/60 after the preceding level passes and touchdown is recorded.
+
+With `tdoc.rtmo.initial_navigation.ground_calibration_seconds: 5.0`, startup
+collects a sealed, same-session stationary/disarmed/zero-throttle IMU interval.
+It initializes the existing MESA gyro/accelerometer bias inputs once. Raw samples
+remain unchanged; FCU position/attitude do not re-anchor MESA. A missing, moving,
+expired or foreign-session calibration is rejected. This is initialization, not
+evidence of dynamic estimator or hover accuracy.
+
+Any Python/configuration change covered by the model identity requires a fresh
+compatible Offline handoff before Online reuse. Do not edit certificate hashes,
+reset, refresh forcing or clear KStore after accepting that handoff. Short
+diagnostic Offline runs used during integration do not demonstrate a completed
+Offline flight mission.
+
+This profile is an integration test, not an accepted hover result. The measured
+Native outcome, remaining gates, source patch, hashes and screenshots are in
+`integration_hover_20261104_1710/FINAL_NATIVE_REPORT_FA.html`. Opening panels or
+reaching ARM alone does not pass the closed-loop flight test.
+
